Lay-What: Each blog post now shows a short row of share icons under the title.
Lay-How: Tap an icon to copy the link or open that site. A check mark shows the copy worked.
Lay-Why: The old named buttons used the top of a phone screen, so the article started lower.
Tech-What: The blog post page draws one icon row. The words are the accessible name and the tooltip.
Tech-How: The row is inline icons, 32px, that wrap only when they no longer fit. A successful copy swaps in a check for 1.6 seconds.
Tech-Why: Named buttons wrapped onto extra lines on a narrow screen, pushing the article down.
